    "proved": "A complete geodesic polar-total-variation metric separates the ordinary models on the divisorial product locus, where every pair has zero top-volume comparison. Ideal models are a closed geodesically convex analytic closure; ideal projection is the unique nearest-point 1-Lipschitz retraction, with diffuse polar mass as distance. Metric convergence gives L1 convergence upstairs for every smooth positive volume form.",
    "mechanism": "The exact product-envelope identities make the product map an isometry from the complete curve model space. Rank deficiency forces all three volumes in top-degree comparison to vanish. Finite rational atomic approximations, with the unit divisor coefficient, clear local monomial denominators and give analytic density; analytic envelope equality proves the converse. Fubini against smooth fiber-integrated densities transfers L1 convergence.",
    "retained_boundary": "This metric is only on the specified product locus. No general higher-dimensional completion, capacity assertion upstairs, nonclosed metric extension or background-compatibility theorem is claimed."
